From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:20:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Dust indoors and out, and a wind outdoors

Patch 0036 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-08, on the dust of patch 0035: "outside versus inside to have their own dust
settings. So that way, outside, I may want a light setting with low density, whereas inside of a
cavern or inside the Temple of Time, I might want some more dust floating around"; "set the density
levels and visibility levels"; "wind gusts or whatever outside ... interior rooms should not have
that"; "what direction it's going, if there's wind"; "Full control over exactly how that interacts
both indoors and outdoors".

Two parameter groups join the block after tuneExperiment, four wide and aligned the same way on
both sides: tuneDust (the indoor dust's density and visibility, the outdoor dust's density and
visibility) and tuneWind (the way the wind blows over the ground as world x and z, its speed in
world units a second, its gusts). The indoor drift's pace takes 0035's spare slot,
tuneReflection.w, and 0035's one value is gone from the configuration.

The air pass picks the place's dust by the game's own light mode: indoors the motes only wander
about their places at the drift's pace; outdoors the whole field of motes travels with the wind,
its speed rising and easing with the gusts (never turning back), each mote wandering a little as it
goes, and outdoor motes show against the open sky as well as in front of a surface. A density is
the share of the air's cells that hold a mote; a visibility is a lit mote's brightness as a share
of the light on it. Either at 0 turns that place's dust off.

